MLA Standard: MLA.GEO.CIR.7
Question:
A 45° sector has radius 10. What coefficient of pi gives the sector area?
{
~A. 10pi#This uses the radius but does not square it or use the angle fraction.
~B. 45pi#This uses the angle as an area coefficient.
=C. 12.5pi#Use 45/360(pi10?), so the coefficient of pi is 12.5.
~D. 2.5pi#This coefficient comes from arc length, not sector area.
}
